# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 9 (a supplier's `@ !event` answers each firing a tick late, so the request of tick 1 is accepted in tick 2) and Part III ch. 6 (the response is the player's); the tick the label moves in is a guess a real run may correct.
test moved_once

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="move")
    2: Ui.Label(text="the seat heard nothing yet")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click

tick 2
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="the seat heard accepted")
